[h2]Batch Open Containers (Multi-Select)[/h2]
Honestly, this is just a tiny, pretty useless little mod—nothing fancy at all. It is literally because I felt like if you can marquee-select a bunch of containers at once, being able to open them all together with right-click just makes sense. Turns out it can actually come in handy when brewing batches of wine (and yes, it works on [b]box-selected machines[/b] too).

[list]
[*][b]Box-Select & Right-Click Open All[/b]: Drag with Left-Click to box-select 2 or more openable items, then Right-Click any one of them to pop open the normal context menu. The [b]Open[/b] button becomes [b]Open All (N)[/b]—click it to open every selected openable window in one go. (Hold [b]Shift + Right-Click[/b] if you ever want the regular single-item Open button.)
[*][b]Works on Wine Bottles, Containers & Machines[/b]: Applies to any owned item that has an openable window—unfermented wine bottles, backpacks, storage crates, safes, and also [b]multiple box-selected machines[/b] (vending machines, battery hubs, cages, processors, etc.).
[*][b]Keeps Remembered Positions by Default[/b]: Windows that already have a saved position restore right where you left them; newly opened windows without saved positions are automatically tiled neatly from the top-left (or cascaded / vanilla, configurable in Options) so they do not stack on top of each other. What you see in the preview GIF is the default Tile layout.
[*][b]Optional Direct Mode[/b]: Prefer skipping the menu altogether? Enable [b]Right-click directly opens all selected[/b] under Options (holding Shift + Right-Click still brings up the context menu).
[/list]

[h3]Options[/h3]
Configurable anytime under [b]Options -> Batch Open[/b]:
[list]
[*][b]Right-click directly opens all selected[/b] (default: Off): When enabled, right-clicking a selected openable item opens all selected targets immediately instead of showing the context menu.
[*][b]Batch open window layout[/b] (default: Tile): Choose [b]Tile (Grid)[/b], [b]Cascade (Staggered)[/b], or [b]Vanilla Position[/b] for newly batch-opened windows.
[*][b]Keep remembered window positions[/b] (default: On): Restores previously remembered positions and only arranges unpositioned windows; turn off to arrange all newly opened windows in the batch together.
[/list]

[h3]Compatibility & Notes[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]Menu-Safe[/b]: Updates the vanilla [b]Open[/b] button label and click behavior directly without rebuilding the context menu tree, so it stays compatible with mods that customize the right-click menu.
[*][b]Save-safe & Zero Sensitive Capabilities[/b]: Pure input/UI convenience mod; does not alter saves and requires no external-reflection capability (Capabilities is empty).
[/list]

